 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Pure lisse relative affine-curve step",
 "statement": "Fix the coefficient and weight conventions of\n[def-weil-punctual-weights]. Let $h:U_0\\to Y_0$ be a\nsmooth separated morphism\nbetween separated finite-type\n$k_0$-schemes, with every nonempty geometric fiber a smooth affine\ncurve. Let $\\mathcal F$ be a\nlisse\n$\\Qlb$-Weil sheaf that is\npunctually $\\iota$-pure of weight $w$.\nThen for every $i$, $R^ih_!\\mathcal F$ is $\\iota$-mixed of weights\nat most $w+i$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-p-dl-general-relative-line/thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core.md",
  "place": "node thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core, order 2844"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-punctual-weights",
  "def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions",
  "def-weil-scheme-morphism-properties",
  "def-weil-weil-sheaf-complex",
  "def-pod-lisse-l-adic-sheaves",
  "def-weil-integral-rational-qbar-compact-support",
  "def-weil-derived-cohomology-sheaves"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Fix a cohomological degree $i$ and put $\\mathcal G_i=R^ih_!\\mathcal F$. Apply [lem-zl-relative-curve-mixedness] to the given $h$ and $\\mathcal F$: the base and source are separated and of finite type over the fixed finite field, $h$ is smooth and separated, every nonempty geometric fiber is a smooth affine curve, and $\\mathcal F$ is lisse and punctually $\\iota$-pure of weight $w$, exactly as required there. Obtain a real number $u_i$ for which $\\mathcal G_i$ is $\\iota$-mixed of weights at most $u_i$. In particular it is a constructible $\\Qlb$-Weil sheaf and has a finite filtration by constructible Weil subsheaves with punctually pure quotients; these are part of the meaning of mixedness in [def-weil-punctual-weights]. No lissity of $\\mathcal G_i$ is asserted.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-zl-relative-curve-mixedness",
    "def-weil-punctual-weights"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-p-dl-general-relative-line/thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof: the curve-reduction lemma supplies a finite mixed filtration"
   }
  },
  {
   "text": "Apply [lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual] to the same morphism and pure lisse sheaf. For every closed point $y$ of degree $m$, each local Frobenius eigenvalue $\\alpha$ on $(\\mathcal G_i)_{\\bar y}$ satisfies $|\\iota(\\alpha)|\\le(q^m)^{(w+i)/2}=q_y^{(w+i)/2}$, with $q_y=\\#\\kappa(y)=q^m$. Thus the punctual upper bound holds for the very same sheaf $\\mathcal G_i$ shown mixed in step 1, with the same geometric-Frobenius and coefficient conventions.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-p-dl-general-relative-line/thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof: first sentence, the punctual eigenvalue bound"
   }
  },
  {
   "text": "Apply [lem-zl-mixed-punctual-cutoff] with $Y_0$ the given base, $\\mathcal G=\\mathcal G_i$, $u=u_i$, and $v=w+i$. Its constructibility and finite mixed-filtration hypothesis are supplied by step 1; its bound at every closed point is supplied by step 2. The base is separated and finite type, and the finite field, embedding $\\iota$, coefficient field and local Frobenius operators agree throughout. The conclusion is that $R^ih_!\\mathcal F$ is $\\iota$-mixed of weights at most $w+i$. Since $i$ was arbitrary, this proves the assertion in every degree. The cutoff is applied to an existing filtration by Weil subsheaves, so no gluing of stalkwise filtrations is used.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-zl-mixed-punctual-cutoff"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-p-dl-general-relative-line/thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof: apply the punctual cutoff with v=w+i; final sentence"
   }
  }
 ],
